// SH27: host browser/game delete policy off ui.kab. import "kab/ui/ui_host"
// Do not grow ui.kab. Do not delete runtime/browser* until smoke is complete.
// Product logic is Kab-owned (nav/session/load_policy/theme hooks) and the
// kb_* native surface is frozen (KB-H1 gate `sh27_kb_h1_frozen_native_surface`
// audits mod.rs against the allowlist). Document pipeline is Kab-owned now:
// kv8/module splits sections + kdom/markup builds the DOM via the provider
// hook, and krender/displaylist produces draw ops in Kab on the paint frame.
// Host capability in Rust: fetch I/O, rasterize→pixels, window/input pump,
// framebuffer present (kframe_present_ops rasterizes the Kab display ops).
// uiHostDeleteOk flipped true after the SH27 production probe
// (examples/sh27/sh27_ui_production_probe.kab) returned streak=8 on
// `kabootar run`: every sweep proved (1) the Kab display list feeds the
// framebuffer — kdom/document.paint presents krender/displaylist ops so the
// published compositor frame carries backend "kab-displaylist" — and
// (2) kv8 script eval runs on lib/kv8 — navGo loads a .kv8 module and
// kb_run_kv8 routes it through kv8RunPage (evalRoute["kab"] increments).

pub fn uiHostDeleteOk() {
    return true
}
